POSITION SUMMARY
Bandai Namco Entertainment America Inc. (BNEA) embraces the idea of Fun 
For
 All 
Into
 the Future, where anything is possible for our fans and team, using technology and innovation to create the most memorable and genuine experiences around our brands. Creativity is at the heart of all we do, and our talented team works collaboratively to deliver unparalleled levels of insights to inform strategy and strengthen our outcomes
.&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Bandai Namco Entertainment America’s Associate Digital Sales Manager will proactively support in driving digital revenue through effective discount planning / life-cycle management (LCM) across the company’s portfolio on the various digital platforms. They will collaborate with team members, overseas offices, First Party (1P) partners such as Microsoft, Nintendo, Sony, or Valve, and third-party (3P) partners to develop digital SKU plans and execute discount strategies based on industry best practices and internal policies.&nbsp;
Join us at our new campus in Irvine, California where a hybrid work schedule will be observed.&nbsp;
ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Responsible for the planning and execution of digital sales / LCM on all titles for assigned digital platforms to maximize revenue&nbsp;
Collaborate and communicate consistently with overseas Bandai Namco Group companies to ensure global consensus on various discount planning and LCM strategies.&nbsp;
Facilitate regular meetings with assigned 1P and 3P partners to ensure alignment of goals and timelines&nbsp;
Accountable for managing relevant LCM-related matters, including submitting promo lineups into 1P portals and internal approval workflows, and keeping a pulse on 1P post-launch opportunities and curated placements&nbsp;
Maintain understanding of all discounts and performance linked to digital storefront placements for all major platforms&nbsp;
Gather sales-related data, collaborate with internal analytics teams to understand digital trends, report the outcomes of digital promotions, and provide insights as needed&nbsp;
Coordinate with internal teams to determine pricing for all digital storefronts, and provide recommendations for when to advance to the next discount level&nbsp;
Accountable for executing LCM for 3P digital business with digital game distributors such as Humble Bundle or Nuuvem&nbsp;
Responsible for documenting business schemes of other publishers that relate to the games published by Banda
